WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:06.640
Clara Tucker came at midterm and was the head of the department then,

2
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.280
and it was over in Prescott Hall, which is right next to Allen Hall.

3
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:17.540
We were . . . The Home Ec Department was upstairs in Prescott Hall.

4
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.340
Ag Economics was downstairs.

5
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:25.700
When Clara Tucker came, things just popped and home ec just grew by leaps and bounds,

6
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:33.520
because she was a very visionary person and was able to bring in new faculty.

7
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.700
And in the four years that I was there,

8
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:44.980
home economics was quite different from the prior four years, let’s say, because of all the new influences.

9
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:56.380
But I was there when they started the Institutional Foods Program, and they started that in what’s now Pleasant Hall.

10
00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:03.560
It was Smith Hall at that time; they had it in the basement and they started Food Service and the Institutional Foods Program.

11
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:12.720
So I was majoring in this Food Nutrition area and this was during the war years, when the boys were leaving the campus quickly.

12
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:19.440
I remember going home on the weekend and coming back after a busy,

13
00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:26.900
busy, busy weekend, getting into a Quantity Foods class that Monday morning, grating carrots.

14
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.820
I’ll never forget that, grating those carrots.

15
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.620
I thought, “I’ll never get through with these carrots.” [laughs]
